add(1,
'The diagrams show how a modern landfill for household waste is built, used and finally closed.',
'Overall, the landfill is a man-made hole with protective layers and a drainage system. Waste is placed inside the hole, which is covered with clay when it is full, while gases can leave through a pipe.',
'First, a large hole is dug in natural rock. A layer of clay is placed along its sides and bottom, and a synthetic substance is added as another protective layer. Drainage pipes are then installed at the bottom of the hole. These pipes are connected to a drainage tank, forming the system needed before the landfill can be used.',
'During use, household waste is put into the prepared hole. Liquid from the waste collects towards the bottom, where the drainage system is located. Once the landfill has reached the closure stage, the waste is covered with a layer of clay. The waste remains below this cover, and gases are able to pass out through the pipe shown on the right-hand side.',
'Bốn hình gồm hai bước xây dựng, sử dụng và đóng bãi; không thêm xử lý hóa học ngoài hình.',
'Body 1: đào hố, lớp lót và thoát nước. Body 2: sử dụng và đóng bãi.',['process-overview','process-order','location'],{'stages':['construction: hole','construction: lining and drainage','use','closure']})
hold(2,'Câu hỏi ghi 1971–2006 nhưng trục biểu đồ kéo đến 2011; cần xác nhận phạm vi và đơn vị trước khi cố định bài mẫu.')
add(3,
'The diagram shows the main parts of a central heating system in a house and how the system operates.',
'Overall, the system uses a boiler and a pump to send hot water around the house. It includes a storage tank, pipes and several radiators, and it also provides hot water for the taps.',
'Cold water enters the house through a pipe near the roof. A small water tank is located at the top of the building to fill the storage tank below it. An overflow pipe is also shown beside this upper part of the system. The storage tank is connected to the boiler, which is placed lower down in the house and is powered by either gas or oil.',
'The boiler heats the water, and the pump moves hot water through the pipes to the radiators. These radiators are positioned in different parts of the house and are connected by small tubes. After passing through the heating circuit, cooler water returns towards the boiler to be heated again. A separate connection from the storage tank supplies hot water to the household taps.',
'Thiết bị có hai chức năng: sưởi qua radiator và cấp nước nóng cho vòi. Không thêm nhiệt độ hoặc số phòng.',
'Body 1: bộ phận, nguồn nước. Body 2: tuần hoàn nước và vòi.',['process-overview','process-order','location'],{'components':['water tank','storage tank','overflow pipe','boiler (gas or oil)','pump','radiators','taps']})
add(4,
'The table compares the value of New Zealand kiwi fruit exports to five countries in 2010, 2011 and 2012, measured in New Zealand dollars.',
'Overall, Japan was by far the largest market in all three years, followed by China. Export values increased in these two countries and Russia, whereas the figures for Mexico and Saudi Arabia ended below their starting levels.',
'Exports to Japan were worth $271.1 million in 2010, after which they rose to $287.4 million in 2011 and $325.3 million in 2012. A similar increase was seen in China, where the value went from $74.9 million to $84.8 million before reaching $94 million. These two markets were much larger than the other three throughout the period.',
'In contrast, the value for Mexico fell from $6 million to $2.4 million, before recovering to $3.3 million in 2012. Russia recorded steady growth across the three figures, from $968,000 to $1.585 million and then $2.404 million. Saudi Arabia remained the smallest market: exports initially rose from $290,000 to $407,000, but then dropped sharply to just $82,000.',
'Nhật lớn nhất, Trung Quốc thứ hai; Mexico giảm rồi hồi; Saudi Arabia nhỏ nhất. Giữ NZ$, không nhầm triệu/nghìn.',
'Body 1: hai thị trường lớn Nhật–Trung. Body 2: ba thị trường nhỏ.',['intro','overview-trend','sequence','similar'],{'years':[2010,2011,2012],'unit':'NZD','Japan':[271100000,287400000,325300000],'China':[74900000,84800000,94000000],'Mexico':[6000000,2400000,3300000],'Russia':[968000,1585000,2404000],'Saudi Arabia':[290000,407000,82000]})
add(5,
'The diagram shows how organic waste can be recycled in a container to produce compost for use in a garden.',
'Overall, the process involves preparing a suitable container, adding waste and other materials, and leaving the mixture to form compost. It takes six months before the final product is ready for the garden.',
'First, a plastic container with a capacity of two cubic metres is prepared. There are openings in its sides so that air can move in and out. Organic waste is then placed inside in separate layers. Food waste forms the bottom layer, grass is put above it, and newspaper is added on top. The diagram marks the food and grass layers as 15 centimetres deep each.',
'Next, nitrogen and water are added to the waste, with the instruction that only hot water should be used. The container is then covered with a lid. Heat is shown leaving the container while the material remains inside. After a period of six months, the waste has become compost at the bottom of the container. This finished material can then be taken out and used in the garden.',
'Nêu thùng 2 m³, food–grass–newspaper, nitrogen và hot water, chờ 6 tháng; không tự thêm khuấy đảo.',
'Body 1: thùng và lớp nguyên liệu. Body 2: bổ sung, ủ và thành phẩm.',['process-overview','process-order','location'],{'container_m3':2,'months':6,'layers':['food','grass','newspaper']})
hold(6,'Câu hỏi ghi sản lượng thép bằng million tonnes nhưng trục nhỏ khó đọc và giá trị lên đến hàng nghìn. Cần đối chiếu ảnh rõ đơn vị/số để tránh bài mẫu sai.')
add(7,
'The maps show the changes that took place in Felixstone in the UK between 1967 and 2001.',
'Overall, the town gained more tourist facilities, while farmland and some coastal facilities were removed. The golf course and the main road layout remained, but the coastline was used differently by the end of the period.',
'In the upper part of the maps, the golf course stayed in the same position to the left of the high street. The shops on the left of the high street remained, while those on the right were replaced by apartments. Farmland further to the right was replaced by a hotel, with a swimming pool beside it and tennis courts below it. This created a new group of leisure facilities away from the beach.',
'Near the coast, the hotel and cafe remained, and a car park was added beside the hotel. The fish market, marina and pier shown in 1967 were no longer present in 2001. The later map instead shows a public beach in the central area and a private beach further to the right. Wind turbines were also added near the dunes on the left-hand side.',
'Đổi farmland thành cụm hotel/pool/tennis; ven biển bỏ fish market, marina, pier. Không tự gán Bắc khi bản đồ không có la bàn.',
'Body 1: phần trên và high street. Body 2: dải ven biển.',['map-change','map-overview','location'])
add(8,
'The maps compare an existing road system with a proposed layout designed to reduce accidents in the area.',
'Overall, the main planned changes are a new roundabout and traffic lights. Access to the supermarket will change, and the southern connection from Low Lane to Forest Road will close, while the school and houses will remain.',
'In the current layout, a main road runs diagonally through the area, and City Road crosses it. A school is located above City Road on the left, while a row of houses stands below it. The supermarket is on the opposite side of the main road. Several accident locations are marked around the junction and along the nearby sections of road.',
'Under the proposed plan, the central crossing will be replaced by a roundabout, with a separate access route to the supermarket. Traffic lights will be installed where Low Lane meets City Road near the school. Low Lane will no longer connect to Forest Road at its southern end. The school and houses will remain in place. These are proposed changes, so the map does not show actual accident figures after construction.',
'Đây là đề dự kiến thay đổi: dùng will be. Không khẳng định kế hoạch đã giảm tai nạn hay tự cho số liệu hiệu quả.',
'Body 1: bố cục hiện tại. Body 2: vòng xoay và lối vào mới.',['map-change','map-overview','location'])
hold(9,'Ảnh không ghi đơn vị thời gian trên trục tung (giờ/tuần hay cách đo khác). Cần xác nhận đơn vị trước khi đưa bài mẫu định lượng vào chế độ học thuộc.')
add(10,
'The line graph shows the percentage of people in four age groups who went to the cinema once a month in Great Britain between 1984 and 2000.',
'Overall, cinema attendance increased in all four groups over the period. People aged 15–24 had the highest percentages throughout, while those aged 35 and over consistently recorded the lowest figures.',
'Among 15–24-year-olds, the proportion started at about 17% in 1984 and rose to 30% in 1989. It then increased further to 40% in 1994 and approximately 55% in 1999, before ending at around 58%. The figure for children aged 7–14 also rose, from 10% to about 37% between 1984 and 1999, but fell to roughly 32% in the final year.',
'The percentage for the 25–35 age group began at approximately 4%. It increased to around 25% in 1994, remained at that level in 1999, and then reached about 32% in 2000, matching the youngest group. Meanwhile, attendance among people aged 35 and over grew from around 1% to 5% between 1984 and 1994, before reaching roughly 15% by the end.',
'Cả bốn nhóm tăng đầu–cuối; 15–24 cao nhất. Dữ liệu ảnh: nhóm 15–24 bắt đầu khoảng 17%, không lấy 26% từ phần ghi chép PDF.',
'Body 1: hai nhóm trẻ 7–14 và 15–24. Body 2: 25–35 và 35+.',['intro','overview-trend','sequence','from-to'],{'years':[1984,1989,1994,1999,2000],'unit':'percent','approximate':True,'15–24':[17,30,40,55,58],'7–14':[10,18,27,37,32],'25–35':[4,12,25,25,32],'35+':[1,2,5,11,15]})
add(11,
'The line graph compares spending on books in Germany, France, Italy and Austria between 1995 and 2005, in millions of US dollars.',
'Overall, spending increased in all four countries over the period. Germany remained the largest spender, while Austria experienced the greatest overall rise and moved above Italy by the final year.',
'Germany spent about $80 million on books in 1995. This figure rose to $90 million in 1999, before falling slightly to around $85 million in 2003 and then reaching approximately $95 million in 2005. France showed a more consistent upward pattern, with spending increasing from about $55 million to $60 million between 1995 and 1999, and then to roughly $75 million at the end.',
'Italy began at $50 million and increased to around $55 million in 1997, but returned to $50 million two years later. Spending then recovered gradually to just over $60 million in 2005. Austria had the lowest initial figure, at $30 million. It rose to $40 million in 1999 and stayed unchanged in 2001, before climbing sharply to about $70 million by 2005.',
'Tất cả tăng đầu–cuối; Đức luôn lớn nhất; Áo tăng mạnh nhất. Dùng US$ million, không phải số sách.',
'Body 1: Germany và France. Body 2: Italy và Austria.',['intro','overview-trend','sequence','from-to'])
hold(12,'Lời đề nói bar charts và line graph nhưng ảnh chỉ có một biểu đồ về những điểm tốt của London. Thiếu phần còn lại, chưa thể soạn full bài đúng toàn đề.')
add(13,
'The bar chart compares the percentage of households with no car, one car, or two or more cars in a European country in 1971, 1981, 1991 and 2001.',
'Overall, the proportion of households without a car declined, while car ownership became more common. One-car households formed the largest group in the final two years, replacing households with no car as the leading category.',
'In 1971, approximately 47% of households had no car, compared with around 35% owning one car and 16% owning at least two. Ten years later, the share without a car had fallen to about 42%. The figure for one-car households also decreased, to roughly 31%, whereas the proportion with two or more cars increased to approximately 28%.',
'By 1991, one-car ownership had risen sharply to about 47%, the highest figure shown for this category. At the same time, the shares with no car and at least two cars were around 30% and 21% respectively. In 2001, the one-car figure fell slightly to roughly 43%, but it remained the largest category. The other two groups were almost equal, at around 28% each.',
'Ba nhóm theo số xe/hộ; no car giảm, one car lớn nhất về cuối. Giá trị đọc xấp xỉ từ cột.',
'Dưới 4 nhóm: Body 1 cho 1971–1981, Body 2 cho 1991–2001.',['intro','overview-trend','compare','respectively'])
add(14,
'The table shows the number of cars produced in Argentina, Australia and Thailand in 2003, 2006 and 2009.',
'Overall, production increased in Argentina but declined in Australia. Thailand produced by far the most cars in all three years, although its output fell after reaching a peak in 2006.',
'In 2003, Thailand manufactured 735,852 cars, compared with 452,163 in Australia and 235,088 in Argentina. Over the next three years, Thai production rose sharply to 1,162,356 vehicles. A similar change was seen in Argentina, where the figure increased to 352,759. In contrast, the number of cars made in Australia fell to 341,268, putting it slightly below Argentina in 2006.',
'Between 2006 and 2009, Argentina continued to increase its production, reaching 466,089 cars. This was almost twice its figure at the start of the period. Meanwhile, output in Thailand dropped to 999,963 vehicles, but remained above the 2003 level and higher than the combined total for the other two countries. Australia recorded a further decline to 245,624 cars, leaving it with the lowest output in the final year.',
'Thailand luôn cao nhất; Argentina tăng liên tục, Australia giảm. Đã dùng số từ ảnh: 452,163 và 466,089, khác một số chữ số trong PDF.',
'Dưới 4 nhóm: Body 1 từ 2003 đến 2006; Body 2 từ 2006 đến 2009.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','similar','peak'],{'years':[2003,2006,2009],'unit':'cars','Argentina':[235088,352759,466089],'Australia':[452163,341268,245624],'Thailand':[735852,1162356,999963]})
hold(15,'Ảnh thiếu câu hỏi đầy đủ và quốc gia; tổng các tỷ lệ theo tuổi vượt 100%. Cần xác nhận mẫu số (tỷ lệ trong mỗi nhóm tuổi hay phân bố tuổi) trước khi viết intro và diễn giải số liệu.')
add(16,
'The diagram shows how rainwater is collected and treated so that it can be used as drinking water in an Australian town.',
'Overall, rainwater is gathered from the roofs of houses and passes through a filter and two tanks. After chemical treatment, the water is sent back to the houses for people to drink.',
'At the beginning of the process, rain falls onto the roofs of the houses. It runs down through drains attached to the buildings and enters an underground pipe. This pipe connects the houses to a water filter. The collected rainwater passes through the filter before flowing into a storage tank, where it is kept ahead of the next treatment stage.',
'Water then leaves the storage tank through another pipe and enters a separate water treatment tank. Chemicals are added at this stage, as shown by the small container above the tank. Once treatment is complete, the water flows along a supply pipe leading back towards the houses. It is carried upwards into each building, where it comes out of the taps as drinking water.',
'Theo mũi tên: roof/drain → filter → storage → treatment + chemicals → drinking water. Không thêm tên hóa chất hoặc khẳng định loại bỏ chất cụ thể.',
'Body 1: thu gom, lọc và chứa. Body 2: xử lý và cấp nước.',['process-overview','process-order','location'],{'sequence':['roofs','drains','water filter','storage','chemical treatment','drinking water']})
add(17,
'The two pie charts compare the shares of the world’s forests and timber in five regions: South America, Africa, Asia, Europe and North America.',
'Overall, Africa and North America accounted for the largest shares of forest, while North America had the greatest share of timber. Africa showed the clearest difference between the two charts, with a large forest share but a very small timber share.',
'Africa contained 27% of the world’s forests, slightly more than North America at 25%. Europe accounted for 18%, while the figures for South America and Asia were lower, at 16% and 14% respectively. Together, Africa and North America therefore represented just over half of the forest shown in the first chart.',
'In terms of timber, North America had the highest proportion, at 30%, followed by South America at 23%. Europe accounted for 20%, which was slightly above its forest share. Asia’s share was 18%, four percentage points above its forest figure. By contrast, Africa accounted for only 9% of timber, despite having the largest share of forest among the five regions. Its timber share was therefore only one third of its forest share.',
'Hai biểu đồ tĩnh: forest so với timber. Không gọi timber là tốc độ khai thác hoặc suy ra nguyên nhân.',
'Body 1: tỷ lệ forest. Body 2: timber và đối chiếu.',['intro','static-overview','compare','respectively'],{'unit':'percent','regions':['South America','Africa','Asia','Europe','North America'],'forest':[16,27,14,18,25],'timber':[23,9,18,20,30]})
add(18,
'The plans compare the current layout of an office building with a proposed design for the future.',
'Overall, the building will gain more space for meetings and outdoor seating. The kitchen and canteen will be replaced by offices, and the grass areas on both sides will be used for other purposes.',
'At present, the kitchen, canteen and storeroom are arranged along the upper side of the building. Four small offices stand in a row along the lower side, with open space between the two rows. There is a WC near the right-hand side, and grass lies outside both sides of the building. Entrances are shown on the left and at the bottom.',
'In the future layout, the kitchen and canteen will become two offices, while the storeroom will remain in place. The offices along the bottom will be reorganised into two larger rooms, with the lower entrance between them. An outdoor seating area will replace grass on the upper left. On the right, there will be a meeting area, and a coffee machine will be added near the WC.',
'Bản đồ tương lai: will be; so sánh kitchen/canteen, offices, grass và meeting area. Không gọi kế hoạch là đã hoàn thành.',
'Body 1: hiện tại. Body 2: bố trí tương lai.',['map-overview','map-change','location'])
hold(19,'Câu hỏi ghi million dollars per tons cho giá gạo nhưng trục là khoảng 250–600. Cần xác nhận đơn vị giá; các đường 2013–2015 cũng cần ảnh rõ hơn để gán đúng màu.')
add(20,
'The line graph shows oil consumption in the USA, China, Western Europe and Japan, and the Middle East from 2009 to 2030, in millions of barrels per day.',
'Overall, the USA has the highest consumption throughout the period shown. Its figure is expected to fall after 2015, while China and the Middle East show overall increases. Western Europe and Japan follow a downward trend.',
'In 2009, the USA consumed about 9 million barrels per day, compared with 4 million in Western Europe and Japan. The American figure rises to 10 million in 2015, before falling to 8 million in 2025 and a projected 7.5 million in 2030. Consumption in Western Europe and Japan decreases from 4 million to 3 million in 2015 and is expected to reach 2 million by the end.',
'China and the Middle East both begin at approximately 2 million barrels per day. China’s consumption increases to 3 million in 2015 and 4 million in 2025, before a projected fall to around 3.5 million. The Middle East shows a slower but continuous rise across the points given, reaching 2.5 million in 2025 and an expected 3 million in 2030.',
'USA cao nhất; China và Middle East tăng đầu–cuối; Western Europe & Japan giảm. Mốc 2030 là tương lai, không khẳng định đã quan sát.',
'Body 1: USA và Western Europe & Japan. Body 2: China và Middle East.',['intro','overview-trend','forecast','from-to'],{'years':[2009,2015,2025,2030],'unit':'million barrels/day','USA':[9,10,8,7.5],'China':[2,3,4,3.5],'Western Europe and Japan':[4,3,2.5,2],'Middle East':[2,2,2.5,3]},'Ảnh không đánh dấu ranh giới actual/forecast. Bài dùng thì mô tả biểu đồ ở các mốc giữa và nêu rõ 2030 là dự báo; không gán năm gốc dự báo.')
hold(21,'Các nhóm tuổi không đầy đủ, tỷ lệ cộng lại vượt 100% và nhãn Population Growth không khớp lời đề percentage of population. Chưa rõ mẫu số để diễn giải chính xác.')
add(22,
'The line graph compares the weekly consumption of chicken, beef, lamb and fish in a European country between 1979 and 2004, measured in grams per person.',
'Overall, chicken consumption increased, while the amounts of beef, lamb and fish eaten declined. Chicken became the most consumed item during the period, whereas fish remained the least popular throughout.',
'In 1979, beef consumption stood at about 220 grams per person per week, making it the highest figure. It fluctuated during the following years, but then fell overall to around 110 grams in 2004. Chicken showed the opposite pattern. Its figure started at approximately 150 grams and increased despite some fluctuations, overtaking beef around the late 1980s and reaching about 250 grams at the end.',
'Lamb consumption also began at around 150 grams per person per week. It fell overall, with several short-term rises, and ended at approximately 60 grams in 2004. Fish was consumed in much smaller quantities than the three meats. Its figure decreased from about 60 grams to around 40 grams over the period, and the changes were relatively small compared with those for beef and lamb.',
'Đơn vị grams/person/week; chicken tăng còn ba loại kia giảm. Không dùng amount of people hoặc suy đoán lý do ăn uống.',
'Body 1: chicken và beef đối lập. Body 2: lamb và fish giảm.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','peak'])
add(23,
'The line chart compares the percentage of female members of parliament in Germany, Italy, France, the UK and Belgium between 2000 and 2012.',
'Overall, all five countries ended with higher percentages than they started with. Italy overtook Germany to record the highest figure in 2012, while the UK showed the largest increase and finished at approximately the same level as Belgium.',
'Germany had the highest initial proportion, at about 33% in 2000. Its figure rose gradually to around 37% in 2012. Italy increased more strongly, from approximately 27% to 39%, moving above Germany in the final year. France also followed an upward trend, although its rise was smaller, from about 25% to 32% over the period.',
'The UK began with by far the lowest figure, at roughly 3%. This increased to around 9% in 2004 and 20% in 2008, before reaching approximately 23% in 2012. Belgium started at about 17% and rose to 23% in 2004. After a small further increase in 2008, its figure slipped back to around 23%, leaving it level with the UK at the end.',
'Dùng ảnh đề: Italy cao nhất cuối kỳ, UK bằng Belgium cuối kỳ. Không sao chép nhận định UK luôn thấp nhất từ PDF vì cuối kỳ bằng nhau.',
'Body 1: Germany–Italy–France. Body 2: UK–Belgium.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','similar'],{'unit':'percent','approximate':True,'years':[2000,2004,2008,2012],'Germany':[33,34,35,37],'Italy':[27,31,33,39],'France':[25,27,29,32],'UK':[3,9,20,23],'Belgium':[17,23,24,23]})
hold(24,'Câu hỏi ghi UK 1995–2002 và billions, nhưng biểu đồ ghi Finland 1995–2004 và minutes (millions). Cần chọn nguồn đúng; không sửa âm thầm.')
add(25,
'The pie charts compare how a UK school divided its annual spending among five categories in 1981, 1991 and 2001.',
'Overall, teachers’ salaries took the largest share in every year, while insurance remained the smallest item. Spending on other workers’ salaries declined, whereas the proportions for insurance and furniture and equipment ended higher than they began.',
'Teachers’ salaries accounted for 40% of total spending in 1981. This share increased to 50% in 1991, before falling to 45% in 2001, although it remained the leading category. The proportion spent on other workers’ salaries moved in the opposite overall direction, declining from 28% to 22% and then to 15%. Together, these two salary categories represented 60% of the budget in the final year.',
'Resources such as books received 15% of spending in 1981 and 20% in 1991, but only 9% in 2001. Furniture and equipment followed a different pattern, falling from 15% to 5% before rising sharply to 23%. Meanwhile, insurance grew from just 2% to 3% and then 8%, remaining below all the other categories despite this increase.',
'Teachers’ salaries lớn nhất ở cả 3 mốc; insurance nhỏ nhất. Chỉ mô tả tỷ trọng ngân sách, không khẳng định tổng tiền tăng.',
'Body 1: hai nhóm lương. Body 2: resources, furniture/equipment, insurance.',['intro','overview-trend','sequence','from-to'],{'years':[1981,1991,2001],'unit':'percent','teachers':[40,50,45],'other workers':[28,22,15],'resources':[15,20,9],'furniture/equipment':[15,5,23],'insurance':[2,3,8]})
